Interface (all async): ``create`` ``bulk_create`` ``get`` ``list`` ``update``
``delete`` ``bulk_delete`` ``count`` ``exists``. ``get_repository()`` is the
FastAPI dependency; tests patch it to ``InMemory{{ crud_entity | capitalize }}Repository``.

``bulk_delete`` takes ``Sequence[str]``, not ``list[str]``: once a class defines
a method literally named ``list``, mypy (checked: 2.3.1) misresolves every
*later* bare ``list[...]`` annotation in that same class as a reference to the
method rather than the builtin generic. ``bulk_create``'s ``list[...]`` is
safe because it appears earlier in the class body, before the ``list`` method.
{% if crud_soft_delete %}
Soft delete is on: ``delete``/``bulk_delete`` set ``deleted_at`` instead of
removing the row/doc/hash; ``get``/``list``/``count``/``exists``/``update``
treat a soft-deleted entity as not found.
